     The sseettrruunnnnaabbllee() function is used to change a process's state to be
     runnable.  The process is placed on a runqueue(9) if needed, and the
     swapper process is woken up and told to swap the process in if the
     process is swapped out.  If the process has been asleep for at least one
     run of sscchheeddccppuu(), then uuppddaatteepprrii() is used to adjust the priority of the
     process.

     The uuppddaatteepprrii() function is used to adjust the priority of a process that
     has been asleep.  It retroactively decays the estimated CPU time of the
     process for each sscchheeddccppuu() event that the process was asleep.  Finally,
     it calls rreesseettpprriioorriittyy() to adjust the priority of the process.

